puls.json
.claude/
HANDOFF.md
tests/
# Screenshots. The repo is public and the app is full of real training data, so a debug capture
# dropped in the folder must not be committable by accident — which nearly happened 2026-08-06 when
# a Playwright script wrote its output here via a relative path.
*.png
# screenshots/ is the ONE exception: the README images, generated locally from synthetic data and
# containing nothing personal. The blanket rule above still stands everywhere else, so a stray
# capture at the repo root remains uncommittable — which is the whole point. Regenerate rather than
# hand-place a file here; the folder is named for exactly what belongs in it, so nothing drifts in.
!screenshots/*.png
